  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Cook rice: Fill a medium saucepan three-quarters full with water and bring to the boil. Crumble in 1 stock cube and stir to dissolve. Add the rice and cook for 25-27 mins until tender. Drain.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2273242/photos/large/cook_rice-419b65f95f527aa5b52d14399f949841.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer mushrooms: Meanwhile, put the mushrooms and 310ml (1¼ cups) boiling water in a small saucepan and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to medium-low and cook, covered, for 15 mins or until tender. Reserve 60ml (¼ cup) mushroom cooking liquid, then drain the mushrooms.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2273243/photos/large/simmer_mushrooms-d2dc81e06c55412095b7e5b10be5e58b.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Cut the pak choy into thirds. Thinly slice the tofu. Thinly slice the garlic. Slice the mushroom caps, discarding the stems. To make the sauce, combine 2 tsp cornflour, 1 tbs soy sauce, 1 tsp white vinegar and 1½ tbs water in a bowl.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2273244/photos/large/prep_ingredients-2c156b9b321557e10acb1f64cb24ebbb.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir-fry tofu and veggies: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over high heat. Stir-fry the garlic for 30 secs. Add the pak choy, mushrooms, tofu and cashews and stir-fry for 1 min. Add the sauce and reserved mushroom cooking liquid and stir-fry for 1 min or until heated through. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2273245/photos/large/make_sauce-494349346e9e64e25088e95e4b53e65a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir-fry and serve up: Divide the rice and tofu stir-fry among bowls and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2273246/photos/large/stir_fry_and_serve_up-2227a4e09e4b10429d4ad97244211271.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Did you know?: Shiitake mushrooms have a great meaty flavour and add a touch of smokiness to the dish. Dried shiitakes need to be rehydrated before use, but the cooking liquid adds a wonderful depth of flavour to a recipe when added along with the mushrooms.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2273247/photos/large/did_you_know-91ee1b373840ec9a6fc0cf466f9401d3.jpeg"
    }
  ]
